      "content_license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "body": "@Zibbobz I&#39;d suggest you check carefully all around the edges of the diaper to ensure there&#39;s no rough, plastic type material rubbing uncomfortably against his skin. If a 4 month old is getting distressed by something like this, it seems most likely that something on the diaper is causing physical discomfort. If there&#39;s nothing obvious, then I&#39;d suggest you try different diaper brands, to see if this may help. They vary quite a lot, and we found that even some of the most common brands didn&#39;t work well at all."
